Then $BD = \frac{x}{3/2} = \frac{2x}{3},$ and $CD = \frac{x}{1/2} = 2x,$ so
\[BC = BD + DC = \frac{2x}{3} + 2x = \frac{8x}{3}.\]Since $BC = 32,$ $x = 12.$

Therefore, $[ABC] = \frac{1}{2} \cdot AD \cdot BC = \frac{1}{2} \cdot 12 \cdot 32 = \boxed{192}.$

Let $P$ be the foot of the perpendicular from $F$ to the line containing $AB$. [asy]size(150);
defaultpen(linewidth(0.7) + fontsize(10)); real lsf = 0.6;
pair C = (2,0), B = 2*dir(60), A = 2*dir(120), F = -C, E = -B, D = -A, P = foot(F,A,B), Y = B+(4,0);
draw(A--B--C--D--E--F--cycle); draw(F--P--Y--cycle); draw(rightanglemark(F,P,A,5));
